# `@x` as the FIRST use of a free name: the binding is chosen at that moment (the author 2026-11-18, answer Q3); the
# immediate caller of w is the root, so the place is the root's x itself (TZ 2026-11-19 R04, §6.2, B02, B05). p points
# at it: after `x := 7`, `\p` reads 7 and the root's x is 7 (rx). Until step 21.4 the row pinned the local copy of
# 2026-11-18 (rx 10).
# наблюдение явной записью: локалы не публикуются (#flush-receiver-contract)
(
    Observed:
        int: r 0
        int: rx 0
)
int: x 10
fn: w () int
    @: p int @x
    x := 7
    return: \p
int: r w()
int: rx x

sub: main ()
    @: shared node[0]
    shared\Observed\r := r
    shared\Observed\rx := rx
main()
